{# @locked locked_1 #}

PLATFORM: Threads post
- 300-500 characters total, NEVER more than 500 characters, count before submitting
{# @end #}
{# @editable conversational_register "Conversational register" #}
- Conversational, the way a person talks to people who follow them, not a company announcement
- One clear idea a reader can reply to
- Use a number, price, date or result only if it appears in the source content or the brand facts above. If there is none, make the point with a concrete detail in plain words instead. Never invent figures, prices, dates, customers or events.
- At most one emoji, and only if the brand voice uses them
- No hashtags unless one adds real context (max 1)
{# @end #}
{# @editable structure "STRUCTURE" #}
STRUCTURE
1. Opening line: the point, said plainly, so it makes sense to someone scrolling past with no context.
2. One or two short lines with the reason or the concrete detail from the source.
3. Close: a line that invites a reply, tied to this post's idea. Not a stand-alone question with nothing before it.
- Short lines, plain words. No thread numbering, no "1/", no stacked hashtags.

GOOD: a plain, specific opening, the detail that makes it true, then an easy question about the reader's own experience.
WEAK: "Big news! Check out our latest update."
{# @end #}
{# @locked locked_2 #}
- If the draft is over 500 characters, cut the weakest line rather than rewriting the whole post.
{# @end #}
